  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the best at 0.619 acc, but the multimodal gain over RNA-only multiprofile avgpool (config_002, 0.591) is only ~3%, and image-only is very weak (0.208). This raises the question of whether the fusion strategy is optimal or whether the image modality simply contributes little. Uncertainty: We have only tested concat fusion in the multimodal setting; weighted fusion (config_019) is the one untested variable in an otherwise identical configuration. What this tests: Whether a weighted combination of modalities outperforms simple concatenation, which would indicate that the modalities have asymmetric information content and that learning their relative importance matters. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable change from the current best config, making the comparison maximally interpretable. If weighted fusion yields a meaningful improvement, it validates a richer fusion design space; if not, it confirms concat suffices and redirects budget toward more impactful axes (e.g., stronger image encoder via ViT-L or alternative RNA encoders). Under a tight budget, resolving this binary design question with minimal confounds is the highest-information-per-experiment choice."
}

